.TH elf_header 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_header, elf_header_sections \- Retrieve information from the ELF header

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B uint8_t* elf_header_ident(void* elf);
.B void* elf_header_sections(void* elf);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_header_ident function retrieves the ELF header identification from the given ELF file.

The function takes one parameter:
.I elf
A pointer to the ELF file structure.

The function returns a pointer to the ELF header identification.

.SH elf_header_sections
The .B elf_header_sections function retrieves the sections of the ELF file based on the ELF header.

The function takes one parameter:
.I elf
A pointer to the ELF file structure.

The function returns a pointer to the sections of the ELF file. If the ELF header does not specify a valid section offset, the function returns 0.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_header and .B elf_header_sections functions:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>

int main() {
  // Assume elf is a valid pointer to an ELF file structure
  uint8_t* ident = elf_header_ident(elf);
  printf("ELF Header Identification: ");
  for (int i = 0; i < EI_NIDENT; i++) {
    printf("%02x ", ident[i]);
  }
  printf("\n");

  void* sections = elf_header_sections(elf);
  if (sections != 0) {
    printf("Sections retrieved successfully.\n");
  } else {
    printf("Failed to retrieve sections.\n");
  }

  return 0;
}
.!
